Streaming differences
=====================
No archive scripts execute. Runtime never loads pickle checkpoints, downloads model
files, or uses remote code. Local architecture and original class order retained;
unremapped safetensors keys undergo original legacy-key remapping.
Uniform asset is mandatory when exemptions enabled; invalid/missing NPZ fails closed,
without color fallback. Masks belong to individual camera configuration.
Original detection, masks, assessment, tracking, uniform inheritance/EMA/wearpack
rejection, optional person filter, uniform hysteresis, static memory, merged-box,
exemptions, voting, boot uncertainty, worker gate, absence streak ordering retained.
No future prescan or end-video retrospective revocation: already delivered alerts
cannot be revoked when later uniform/static evidence appears. Pending retries need
current person and item evidence and use current frame boxes. Delivery requires ACK.
Seconds-based expiry uses monotonic time, observation windows count sampled frames.
Stationary-memory medians retain latest 512 observations rather than entire video.
Track, history and inherited-uniform buffers are bounded; historical static-memory
records expire/cap independently of active delivered-event state. Reconnect/reset,
non-increasing timestamps, long gaps or resolution changes start new sessions.
Offline/drawing/export settings are explicitly unsupported in streaming API.
